        <mxCell id="ssmsm" value="Shell or tunnel&lt;br&gt;(Session Manager)" style="sketch=0;outlineConnect=0;fontColor=#232F3E;gradientColor=none;fillColor=#E7157B;strokeColor=#ffffff;dashed=0;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;aspect=fixed;shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=mxgraph.aws4.systems_manager;" vertex="1" parent="region">
          <mxGeometry x="553" y="770" width="64" height="64" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="legend" value="&lt;b&gt;1&lt;/b&gt;  Shoppers open the store over HTTPS. CloudFront is the only public entry point.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2&lt;/b&gt;  CloudFront reaches the internal ALB through a VPC origin; the ALB accepts CloudFront IP ranges only.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3&lt;/b&gt;  The ALB forwards to Envoy on the instance, which routes to the storefront, services and tools.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4&lt;/b&gt;  Admin paths (/grafana /jaeger /feature /loadgen /telemetry) go through Lambda@Edge, which requires a Cognito login. Other spellings and /opamp get 403.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5&lt;/b&gt;  The OTel Collector keeps 60 days on disk (Jaeger, Prometheus, OpenSearch) and archives everything to S3 through a gateway endpoint.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;6&lt;/b&gt;  At boot the instance reads its settings from Parameter Store and clones your fork through the NAT Gateway. No inbound access, no SSH." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#879196;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingTop=8;fontSize=12;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="170" y="1140" width="1520" height="120" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
